From: baseband lane
Subject: 0515 pandora_mpss: ask TrustZone whether it even knows the modem's PAS ids

Two hypotheses are now refuted by hardware evidence from 2026-11-21:

  1. the PAS id is not the problem -- nine ids (4 / 0x26 / 24 / 28 / 34 / 15 / 33 / 63 / 0), including
     pas 0 which cannot exist, all returned a0 0xffcfffbb (-3145797) for the same metadata blob;
  2. shm_bridge_enable is not the problem -- with it added (0513) the call returns a0 0, and the
     very next INIT_IMAGE still returns 0xffcfffbb.

The cheapest question left is whether TrustZone knows these ids at all.  PAS_IS_SUPPORTED
(SCM_FN(2,7)) answers it, and this device's own ADSP probe shows the convention:
`pas_is_supported(36) -> a0 0 a1 0x1`, where 36 then loads successfully -- the answer is in a1.
Upstream returns `!!res.result[0]`, so a non-zero answer means supported.

The probe now asks for 4, 0x26, 13, 36 and 0 first, and prints a0/a1 and supported/NOT supported for
each.  If 38 and 4 come back unsupported the id question reopens; if they are supported and
INIT_IMAGE still refuses, the remaining suspects are the metadata's protection/ownership
(the carveout being assigned to MSS before INIT_IMAGE).

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
index f60d79c..48bb1eb 100755
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
@@ -801,6 +801,19 @@ mp_probe_pas_ids(void)
 	if (!mp_option("pandora_mpss_pas_probe")) {
 		return;
 	}
+	/*
+	 * First ask whether TrustZone even knows these ids: PAS_IS_SUPPORTED (SCM_FN(2,7)) answers in
+	 * a1 on this device -- the ADSP's own probe logs `pas_is_supported(36) -> a0 0 a1 0x1` for an
+	 * id that then loads fine.  Upstream returns `!!res.result[0]`, so a non-zero answer means
+	 * supported.
+	 */
+	static const unsigned asked[] = {4, 0x26, 13, 36, 0};
+	for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(asked) / sizeof(asked[0]); i++) {
+		uint64_t a0 = 0, a1 = 0;
+		pandora_scm_call(SCM_FN(2, 7), SCM_ARGS(1), asked[i], 0, &a0, &a1);
+		printf("PANDORA MPSS: pas_is_supported(%u) -> a0 %#llx a1 %#llx (%s)\n", asked[i], a0, a1,
+		    (a0 == 0 && a1) ? "supported" : "NOT supported");
+	}
 	printf("PANDORA MPSS: probing INIT_IMAGE for %u candidate PAS ids with the DTB's metadata\n",
 	    (unsigned)(sizeof(ids) / sizeof(ids[0])));
 	for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(ids) / sizeof(ids[0]); i++) {
